Note: @test stdlib module
Note:
Note: Exposes the C#-registered test framework surface
Note: (TestFramework.TestFunctions): (test "name" body) defers the
Note: body via LazyType + 5 assertion primitives.
Note:
Note: USAGE: composer wraps the test body with the `lazy(...)` keyword so the
Note: body is captured as a Thunk and deferred until the TestRunner forces it
Note: (matches Flow's strict-by-default semantics — `lazy(...)` is the
Note: canonical opt-in to deferred evaluation per (if), (and), (or)). The
Note: TestRunner walks the registry per-test, wrapping each body invocation
Note: in a SnapshotState/RestoreState guard for hermetic isolation.
Note:
Note:   use "@test"
Note:   (test "two plus two is four" lazy((assertEq 4 (add 2 2))))
Note:   (test "audio identity"        lazy((assertWithinDb buf buf 0.5dB)))

module test

internal proc test (String: name, Lazy<Void>: body)
internal proc assert (Bool: condition)
internal proc assertEq (Void: a, Void: b)
internal proc assertNotesMatch (Sequence: a, Sequence: b)
internal proc assertBytesEqual (Buffer: a, Buffer: b)
internal proc assertWithinDb (Buffer: a, Buffer: b, Decibel: toleranceDb)
